bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_llvm_explicit_integer_to_f64_is_bitcast_2026-11-10, 0, "2026-11-26 aarch64 Linux: cargo test --release -p simple-compiler --features llvm --lib codegen::llvm::functions::casts (LLVM 18, own target dir): explicit_integer_to_f64_is_gated_by_semantic_type, explicit_numeric_f64_casts_emit_verified_x64_ir_and_coff, explicit_numeric_f64_casts_emit_verified_x86_ir_and_coff and tagged_any_and_text_integer_casts_require_runtime_decode PASS; rv32_any_to_i32_and_u32_cast_skips_same_width_trunc fails only because this LLVM 18 has no riscv32 target registered (environment). The cranelift-built 76892f19a3a Stage 2 parses 25 and 100 to 25.0/100.0 and converts i64/i32/u8 to f64 correctly on both backends, but that path does not use the seed LLVM compile_cast. Still pending: a Stage 2 constructed by the seed with --backend=llvm (only one Stage 2 build may run on this host and the slot was taken). Status unchanged."
